@prefix spectra: <https://w3id.org/spectra#> .

<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508035> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a clarification that which priority can be applied or has been applied depend on whether the priority adjustment condition in 5.4.3.1.3 is met;\nThe relevant text is changed to “associated PDCP entity has a priority adjustable SDU” or “if a priority adjustable PDCP SDU is buffered for a logical channel”.\nAdd “by lower layer indication”.\n“if configured” is removed from the conditions on the bit rate query prohibit timer.\nThe parameter name for bit rate query prohibit timer is changed to ul-RateQueryProhibitTimer.\nAdd a field description for the reserved bits.\nAdd a clarification, “in the direction where the UL Rate Control MAC CE is sent”, to the field description." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508088> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In 5.3.5.18.6, delete the case of “for the selected cell in accordance with 5.3.7.3” upon the release of redundant configuration when generating the complete configuration.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nLTM\n\nInter-operability:\nIf NW implements this CR but UE not, there is no inter-operatibility issue found;\nIf UE implements this CR but NW not, there is no inter-operatibility issue found." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508103> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "One editorial change is made, i.e. to insert “of ” between “number” and “TRPs”." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508104> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Parameters for triggering condition of FBS operation are added in MeasConfig IE.\nA new UAI indicating UE preference for FBS operation is introudced" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508176> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change#1: Add sbfd-RO-Type in parameter list in clause 5.1.1.\nChange#2: Add the condition \"configured for the first PRACH occasions\" to the preambleReceivedTargetPower, used in the case that Msg3 is transmitted in non-SBFD symbols." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508177> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change#1: Add RO field in (Enhanced) LTM Cell Switch Command MAC CE in clauses 6.1.3.75 and 6.1.3.75a.\nChange#2: Add RO type selection procedure for (Enhanced) LTM Cell Switch Command MAC CE-based CFRA in clause 5.1.1." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508193> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Adding the word “if” in the sentences:\n\n- For TDD, if the MAC entity is configured with ul-SchedInterval shorter than 10 subframes, the Nth grant shall be ignored if it occurs in a downlink subframe or a special subframe.\n\n- Except for NB-IoT, for TDD, if the MAC entity is configured with semiPersistSchedIntervalUL shorter than 10 subframes, the Nth grant shall be ignored if it occurs in a downlink subframe or a special subframe.\n\nImplementation of this CR from the Rel-14 will not cause interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508195> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The editor’s note has been converted into a real note.\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nMUSIM paging collision avoidance\n\nInter-operability:\nThere are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508196> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The editor’s note has been converted into a real note.\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nMUSIM paging collision avoidance\n\nInter-operability:\nThere are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508197> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The editor’s note has been converted into a real note.\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nMUSIM paging collision avoidance\n\nInter-operability:\nThere are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508256> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify in the MAC that DSR can be triggerd for the PDCP SDUs with some segments have been transmitted in MAC PDU and some segments have not.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA and MR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nDSR\n\nInter-operability:\nThere is no interoperability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508257> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify in the MAC that DSR can be triggerd for the PDCP SDUs with some segments have been transmitted in MAC PDU and some segments have not." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508281> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In the field description of cas-MutingConfig, add reference to clause 6.11.2.2 in TS 36.211.\nChange “No” to “-” in the field descritpion of cas-Muting-5GB capability based on the ASN.1 rules." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508305> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change subcarrierSpacing values for FR1 in IE SCS-SpecificCarrier from \"15 or 30kHz\" to \"15, 30 or 60kHz\".\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR standalone, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\nImpacted functionality:\nsubcarrierSpacing configurations\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to this CR while the UE is not, there might be inter-operability issues because the network may configure a subcarrierSpacing value not supported by the UE.\nIf the UE is implemented according to this CR while the network is not, there are no inter-operability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508306> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change subcarrierSpacing values for FR1 in IE SCS-SpecificCarrier from \"15 or 30kHz\" to \"15, 30 or 60kHz\".\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR standalone, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\nImpacted functionality:\nsubcarrierSpacing configurations\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to this CR while the UE is not, there might be inter-operability issues because the network may configure a subcarrierSpacing value not supported by the UE.\nIf the UE is implemented according to this CR while the network is not, there are no inter-operability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508333> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In RAN2#131, support for IoT TN to IoT NTN was agreed with CRs capturing the Stage 3 details in 36.331 (R2-2506518) and 36.306 (R2-2506651). In this CR, Stage 2 description for this for the IoT TN to IoT NTN is introduced, along with support for E-UTRAN TN to NB-IoT NTN." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508334> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In RAN2#131, support for NR TN to NR NTN was agreed with CRs capturing the Stage 3 details in 38.331 (R2-2506652) and 38.306 (R2-2506650). In this CR, Stage 2 description for NR TN to NR NTN is introduced." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508385> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following corrections were made with this CR.\n9.2.3.1 – LTM execution condition failure actions are also applicable for CLTM, clarified this.\n9.2.3.5.2 - candidate gNB selection and provision of LTM security information is applicable only to inter-gNB LTM. Clarified this.\n9.2.3.7.1 – Miscellaneous corrections to CLTM procedures\n9.2.4 – Miscellaneous editorial corrections to L1 event triggered beam evaluations" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508395> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “3> if uac-BarringFactorForAI3 not included in \"UAC barring parameter\":\n4>\tconsider the access attempt as allowed;” in section 5.3.14.5.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G Architecture options:\nNR SA, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\nImpacted functionality:\nAccess barring check\nInter-operability:\n1. If the network supports the changes and the UE does not, there is no inter-operability issue.\n2. If the UE supports the changes and the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508396> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “3> if uac-BarringFactorForAI3 not included in \"UAC barring parameter\":\n4>\tconsider the access attempt as allowed;” in section 5.3.14.5.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G Architecture options:\nNR SA, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\nImpacted functionality:\nAccess barring check\nInter-operability:\n1. If the network supports the changes and the UE does not, there is no inter-operability issue.\n2. If the UE supports the changes and the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508397> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “3> if uac-BarringFactorForAI3 not included in \"UAC barring parameter\":\n4>\tconsider the access attempt as allowed;” in section 5.3.14.5.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G Architecture options:\nNR SA, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\nImpacted functionality:\nAccess barring check\nInter-operability:\n1. If the network supports the changes and the UE does not, there is no inter-operability issue.\n2. If the UE supports the changes and the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508400> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Modify the index-reference of uplinkTxSwitching-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r16 capability, add “R4 FG 7-6 UL-MIMO coherence capability for dynamic Tx switching between 2CC 1Tx-2Tx switching”, to make it clear this capability is applicable to both 2CC and 3CC 1Tx-2Tx UL Tx switching.\nMove the index-reference “R4 16-6: UL-MIMO coherence capability for dynamic Tx switching between 2Tx-2Tx switching” right before the capability IE uplinkTxSwitching2T2T-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r17 and clarify it is for UL Tx swtiching between 2 bands.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nMIMO coherence capability in UL Tx switching\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, or if the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it may cause confusion that uplinkTxSwitching-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r16 capability is only applicable in 3CC 1Tx-2Tx UL Tx switching, and leads to different understandings at NW and UE sides." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508401> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Modify the index-reference of uplinkTxSwitching-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r16 capability, add “R4 FG 7-6 UL-MIMO coherence capability for dynamic Tx switching between 2CC 1Tx-2Tx switching”, to make it clear this capability is applicable to both 2CC and 3CC 1Tx-2Tx UL Tx switching.\nMove the index-reference “R4 16-6: UL-MIMO coherence capability for dynamic Tx switching between 2Tx-2Tx switching” right before the capability IE uplinkTxSwitching2T2T-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r17 and clarify it is for UL Tx swtiching between 2 bands.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nMIMO coherence capability in UL Tx switching\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, or if the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it may cause confusion that uplinkTxSwitching-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r16 capability is only applicable in 3CC 1Tx-2Tx UL Tx switching, and leads to different understandings at NW and UE sides." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508402> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Modify the index-reference of uplinkTxSwitching-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r16 capability, add “R4 FG 7-6 UL-MIMO coherence capability for dynamic Tx switching between 2CC 1Tx-2Tx switching”, to make it clear this capability is applicable to both 2CC and 3CC 1Tx-2Tx UL Tx switching.\nMove the index-reference “R4 16-6: UL-MIMO coherence capability for dynamic Tx switching between 2Tx-2Tx switching” right before the capability IE uplinkTxSwitching2T2T-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r17 and clarify it is for UL Tx swtiching between 2 bands.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nMIMO coherence capability in UL Tx switching\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, or if the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it may cause confusion that uplinkTxSwitching-PUSCH-TransCoherence-r16 capability is only applicable in 3CC 1Tx-2Tx UL Tx switching, and leads to different understandings at NW and UE sides." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508403> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify in the field description of UplinkTxSwitchingBandParameters-v1700 that, the original note is only applicable when R18 UL Tx switching is not configured by uplinkTxSwitchingMoreBands-r18. And add separate paragraph for the case where R18 UL Tx switching is configured.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nMIMO coherence capability in UL Tx switching\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, or if the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it is unclear which capability should be checked when Rel-17 capability UplinkTxSwitchingBandParameters-v1700 is absent and Rel-18 UL Tx switching is configured by uplinkTxSwitchingMoreBands-r18, this may result in inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508404> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify in the field description of UplinkTxSwitchingBandParameters-v1700 that, the original note is only applicable when R18 UL Tx switching is not configured by uplinkTxSwitchingMoreBands-r18. And add separate paragraph for the case where R18 UL Tx switching is configured.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nMIMO coherence capability in UL Tx switching\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, or if the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it is unclear which capability should be checked when Rel-17 capability UplinkTxSwitchingBandParameters-v1700 is absent and Rel-18 UL Tx switching is configured by uplinkTxSwitchingMoreBands-r18, this may result in inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508425> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Updated the conditional presence to specify that PDCP configuration is always provided when SRB4 is setup.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nQoE\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, NR-DC\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not,\nthere is no issue.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, then the SRB4 addition may fail as the UE can not handle the SRB4 configuration without PDCP config." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508430> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Updated the conditional presence to specify that PDCP configuration is always provided when SRB4 or SRB5 is setup.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nQoE\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, NR-DC\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not,\nthere is no issue.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, then the SRB4/SRB5 addition may fail as the UE can not handle the SRB4/SRB5 configuration without PDCP config." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508512> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The reconfiguration case from Cell DTX/DRX to Cell DTX only and from Cell DTX/DRX to Cell DRX only mode is explicitly captured in addition to the cellDTX-DRX-Config release case.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality: NES\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, EN-DC, NR-DC.\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE might not release the corresponding Cell DTX/DRX configuration upon Cell DTX/DRX mode change.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508513> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The reconfiguration case from Cell DTX/DRX to Cell DTX only and from Cell DTX/DRX to Cell DRX only mode is explicitly captured in addition to the cellDTX-DRX-Config release case.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality: NES\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, EN-DC, NR-DC.\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE might not release the corresponding Cell DTX/DRX configuration upon Cell DTX/DRX mode change.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508515> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Periodic/semi-persistent SRS (except SRS for positioning) is added to the list of signals not transmitted by the UE during cell DRX non-active duration.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality: NES\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, EN-DC, NR-DC.\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there are no interoperability issues.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there are no interoperability issues." .
