<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508524> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Introduction of a new capability to indicate support of redirection in 4.3.15." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508534> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the single SCS per frequency layer restriction in general in Clause 9.2.4 Measurements, and it’s applicable for RRC_IDLE state, RRC_INACTIVE state and RRC_CONNECTED state.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, NR-DC, NE-DC, EN-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nInter-frequency cell re-selection\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the UE may consider the network configuration is incorrect." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508535> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the single SCS per frequency layer restriction in general in Clause 9.2.4 Measurements, and it’s applicable for RRC_IDLE state, RRC_INACTIVE state and RRC_CONNECTED state.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, NR-DC, NE-DC, EN-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nInter-frequency cell re-selection\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the UE may consider the network configuration is incorrect." .
