<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508568> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "•\tUpdating the existing ‘SU-MIMO 8Rx receiver’ capability definition to:\n8Rx receiver\n-\tBaseline 8Rx receiver: 8Rx receivers for MIMO transmissions with support of up to 8 layers with joint 8Rx MIMO detector in FR1\n-\tSimplified 8Rx receiver: 8Rx receivers for MIMO transmissions with support of up to 4 layers with two joint 4Rx MIMO detectors in FR1." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508569> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "•\tUpdating the existing ‘SU-MIMO 8Rx receiver’ capability definition to:\n8Rx receiver\n-\tBaseline 8Rx receiver: 8Rx receivers for MIMO transmissions with support of up to 8 layers with joint 8Rx MIMO detector in FR1\n-\tSimplified 8Rx receiver: 8Rx receivers for MIMO transmissions with support of up to 4 layers with two joint 4Rx MIMO detectors in FR1." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508717> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 5.3.5.3\n- Clarified that UE shall release the scheduling resources configured for LTM once the LTM cell switch procedure is successfully completed\n\nSection 6.3.2\n- Added new fields to configure SR configurations and SR resources to be used during an LTM cell switch\n\nSection 6.3.3\n- Added capability for UE which support this feature" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508718> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 5.3.1 and 5.4.1\n- Clarified that UE shall stop using the SR configuration and PUCCH resources configured in ltm-SchedulingRequestConfig in ReconfigurationWithSync, if any.\n\nSection 5.18.35\n- Clarified that if the SR configuration ID is present in the Enhanced LTM cell switch MAC CE, the UE should consider the related SR configuration during the LTM cell switch procedure.\n\nSection 6.1.3.75 and 6.1.3.75a\n- Added new fields for the SR configuration ID in the legacy LTM Cell Switch Command MAC CE and the enhanced one." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508719> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 4.2.9\n- Introduced a new capability so that UE can indicate whether it supports the indication of the SR periodicity within the LTM cell switch command MAC CE." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508720> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 9.2.3.5.1\n- Clarified that In case of dynamic grant scheduling, the network can include in the cell switch command signalled via a MAC CE the SR configuration ID which indicate to the UE the scheduling request configuration and physical layer resources on PUCCH where the UE may send the scheduling request during an LTM cell switch procedure" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508730> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify which band pairs the UE shall support in case of UL Tx switching with up to 4 bands.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: Standalone\n\nImpacted functionality: UL Tx switching with up to 4 bands\n\nInter-operability: If the network implements the CR and the UE does not, there is no inter-operability issue since it is expected that \"possible band pairs\" should be interpreted as all the band pairs that can be derived from the band combination where UL Tx switching Rel-18 is supported.\n\nIf the UE implements the CR and the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue, there is no inter-operability issue since it is expected that \"possible band pairs\" should be interpreted as all the band pairs that can be derived from the band combination where UL Tx switching Rel-18 is supported." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508737> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Setting timeSinceCHO-Reconfig when the failure is due to radio link failure is updated to the procedural text.\n\nImpact analysis\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRLF Report\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR standalone, NR-DC, NE-DC\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, the UE may set timeSinceCHO-Reconfig to a wrong value, consequently, network will not be able to perform the MRO properly." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508738> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Setting timeSinceCHO-Reconfig when the failure is due to radio link failure is updated to the procedural text.\n\nImpact analysis\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRLF Report\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR standalone, NR-DC, NE-DC\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, the UE may set timeSinceCHO-Reconfig to a wrong value, consequently, network will not be able to perform the MRO properly." .
