<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508740> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "SPR procedural text is updated by changing the thresholdPercentageT304 to thresholdPrecentageT304-SCG\n\nImpact analysis\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRLF Report\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR standalone, NR-DC, NE-DC\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, the is no inter-påerability issue" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508757> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add pmch-TimeInterleaving-N-lastMTCH = 1 as candidate value and clarify value 1 indicates time interleaving is not enabled for the last MTCH service.\nAdd pmch-cyclicShiftAlpha3-r19 in UE capability signalling for alpha3." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508772> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 16.12.7\nAdded text to clarify that the control plane procedures are also performed by the peer remote UE to setup a bidirectional link.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR Sidelink\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSidelink Relays\n\nInter-operability:\n1. If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there will be no inter-operability issues.\n2. If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there are no inter-operability issues.\n3. If one UE is implemented according to the CR and another UE is not, there will be no inter-operability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508773> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 16.12.7\nAdded text to clarify that the control plane procedures are also performed by the peer remote UE to setup a bidirectional link.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR Sidelink\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSidelink Relays\n\nInter-operability:\n1. If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there will be no inter-operability issues.\n2. If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issues.\n3. If one UE is implemented according to the CR and another UE is not, there will be no inter-operability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508800> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Remove the limitation that an element among the list of SRI-PUSCH-PowerControl elements is selected only by the SRI field in DCI." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508801> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Remove the limitation that an element among the list of SRI-PUSCH-PowerControl elements is selected only by the SRI field in DCI." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508877> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify that splitDRB-WithUL-BothDirectIndirect-r18 is for PDCP layer split function.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality\nNR SL Multi-path relay\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf one UE implements the CR but not the other UE, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508879> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify that splitDRB-WithUL-BothDirectIndirect-r18 is for PDCP layer split function.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality\nNR SL Multi-path relay\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf one UE implements the CR but not the other UE, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508882> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "It is clarified in 5.2.2.2.1 that unless required in clause 5.2.2.2.2 to obtain SI over Uu interface when MP is configured, the L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE or RRC_CONNECTED is not required to obtain SI over Uu interface, but it may decide to perform the SI acquisition procedure over Uu interface as defined in clause 5.2.2.3 by UE implementation.\n\nIt is clarified in 5.2.2.2.2 that when a common search space on the active BWP to monitor paging is not configured, a L2 U2N Remote UE is not required to monitor paging occasion for SI modifications and/or PWS notifications and so it obtains the updated system information and SIB6/7/8 from the connected L2 U2N Relay UE as defined in clause 5.8.9.9.3.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR Sidelink\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSidelink Relays\n\nInter-operability:\n1. If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the remote UE configured with CSS in MP may uncessarily peform on-demand SI procedure, or the remote UE configured without CSS in MP may miss the updated system information.\n2. If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there will be no inter-operability issues.\n3. If one UE is implemented according to the CR and another UE is not, there will be no inter-operability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508883> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "It is clarified in 5.2.2.2.1 that unless required in clause 5.2.2.2.2 to obtain SI over Uu interface when MP is configured, the L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE or RRC_CONNECTED is not required to obtain SI over Uu interface, but it may decide to perform the SI acquisition procedure over Uu interface as defined in clause 5.2.2.3 by UE implementation.\n\nIt is clarified in 5.2.2.2.2 that when a common search space on the active BWP to monitor paging is not configured, a L2 U2N Remote UE is not required to monitor paging occasion for SI modifications and/or PWS notifications and so it obtains the updated system information and SIB6/7/8 from the connected L2 U2N Relay UE as defined in clause 5.8.9.9.3.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR Sidelink\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSidelink Relays\n\nInter-operability:\n1. If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the remote UE configured with CSS in MP may uncessarily peform on-demand SI procedure, or the remote UE configured without CSS in MP may miss the updated system information.\n2. If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there will be no inter-operability issues.\n3. If one UE is implemented according to the CR and another UE is not, there will be no inter-operability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508886> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a condition “if the measId is not indicated by the condExecutionCond or the condExecutionCondSCG in an entry of condReconfigList in VarConditionalReconfig in which subsequentCondReconfig is included” for the removal of measId in clause 5.3.5.3.\nAdd the “subsequent CPAC” case in the field description for the IE condReconfigToAddModList and condTriggerConfig.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSubsequent CPAC\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, upon reconfiguration with sync, the UE shall remove the measId associated with the subsequent CPAC execution condition, which shall cause the UE to be unable to perform the evaluation of subsequent CPAC execution condition.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508887> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a condition “if the measId is not indicated by the condExecutionCond or the condExecutionCondSCG in an entry of condReconfigList in VarConditionalReconfig in which subsequentCondReconfig is included” for the removal of measId in clause 5.3.5.3.\nAdd the “subsequent CPAC” case in the field description for the IE condReconfigToAddModList and condTriggerConfig.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSubsequent CPAC\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, upon reconfiguration with sync, the UE shall remove the measId associated with the subsequent CPAC execution condition, which shall cause the UE to be unable to perform the evaluation of subsequent CPAC execution condition.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508908> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1. Remove the ‘(i.e., an area specified as a list of polygon or circle shapes)’ from note 0j of subclause 5.2.4.1" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508943> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following changes are made:\nClarification on MDT mode regarding network-side data collection in section 4.1\nClarification on immediate MDT regarding network-side data collection in section 5.1.2.1\nAddition of UE capability for network-side data collection in section 5.1.4\nSome clarifications on support of network-side data collection in section 5.4.1.5\nClarification on data availability indication and reporting for network-side data collection in section 5.1.2.2" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508952> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "For Sidelink resource allocation scheme 2, change the condition check to:\n “If sl-PRS-MaxNumTransmissions is configured and the number of transmissions of the SL-PRS has not reached the selected maximum number of SL-PRS transmissions”.\n\nFor Sidelink resource allocation scheme 1, add the condition check:\n “If sl-PRS-MaxNumTransmissions is not configured”.\n\nEditorial change: “SL-PRRS” should be “SL-PRS”.\n\nClarify the correct reference for SL-PRS resource request.\n\nImpact analysis:\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\nImpacted functionality:\nSL positioning\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to this CR while the network is not, or\nIf the network is implemented according to this CR while the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue since the correct UE procedure can be inferred from the other parts of the spec or other specs." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508953> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "For Sidelink resource allocation scheme 2, change the condition check to:\n “If sl-PRS-MaxNumTransmissions is configured and the number of transmissions of the SL-PRS has not reached the selected maximum number of SL-PRS transmissions”.\n\nFor Sidelink resource allocation scheme 1, add the condition check:\n “If sl-PRS-MaxNumTransmissions is not configured”.\n\nEditorial change: “SL-PRRS” should be “SL-PRS”.\n\nClarify the correct reference for SL-PRS resource request.\n\nImpact analysis:\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\nImpacted functionality:\nSL positioning\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to this CR while the network is not, or\nIf the network is implemented according to this CR while the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue since the correct UE procedure can be inferred from the other parts of the spec or other specs." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508977> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 5.5.2.1 is updated to reflect actions when speedStatePars is included in measConfig.\nAdd the new section 5.5.x and 5.5.x.y to define speed dependant scaling of measurement related parameters.\nAdd mobility state parameters to MeasConfig and VarMeasConfig.\nadd speedStatePars-r19 to include mobilityStateParameters and the new field timeToTrigger-SF.\nadd the field description of timeToTrigger-SF\nNew UE capability to indicate whether the UE supports the mobility state detection and speed dependent measurement related parameters." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508979> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 4.2.9\nIntroduce a new capability so that UE can indicate whether it supports the mobility state detection and speed dependent measurement related parameters in RRC_CONNECTED as specified in TS 38.331 [9]." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2508993> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Capture that for MR-DC, UE can be configured to report MCG specific UE assistance information if the MN is a gNB and/or SCG specific UE assistance information if the SN is a gNB, if it has preferred time offset for PDCCH monitoring after LP-WUS monitoring.\nCapture that SCG specific UE preferred LP-WUS offset reporting can be configured via SRB1 or SRB3.\nCapture that SCG specific UE preferred LP-WUS offset reporting can be directly transmitted to SN or via a transparent container to the MN." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509042> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In clause 6.3.2, clarify by a field description of referenceLocation that the network configures at most one moving reference location for eventD2 with the same ssbFrequency.\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nStandalone\nImpacted functionality:\nNR-NTN, Measurement\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t if the network supports the change and the UE does not, UE is able to report measurement results of one neighbour cell that fulfills eventD2 entering condition.\n2.\t if the UE supports the change and the network does not, network may configure more than one moving reference location per MO and UE is unable to report measurement results of multiple neighbour cells that fulfills eventD2." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509056> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Replace measIdleValidityDuration with measReselectionValidityDuration  in 5.7.10.3 so that the UE sets the validityStatus properly for NR reselection measurement reporting.\n\nAdd a new field validityStatus-r18 within the IE MeasResultsPerCellIdleEUTRA to allow UE to set validityStatus for reporting valid E-UTRA measurement results.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, NE-DC, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nValidation of reported idle/inactive and reselection measurements\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue but network has no idea how UE checked the reported measurement validity and might configure CA/DC wrongly.\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509061> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "SPR procedural text is updated by changing the thresholdPercentageT304 to thresholdPrecentageT304-SCG\n\nImpact analysis\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRLF Report\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR standalone, NR-DC, NE-DC\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, the is no inter-påerability issue" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509063> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Description on disaster roaming in EPS is added" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509065> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Disaster roaming in EPS is defined as optional UE capability without radio access capabiltiy signaling." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509076> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify which band pairs the UE shall support in case of UL Tx switching with up to 4 bands.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: Standalone\n\nImpacted functionality: UL Tx switching with up to 4 bands\n\nInter-operability: If the network implements the CR and the UE does not, there is no inter-operability issue since it is expected that \"possible band pairs\" should be interpreted as all the band pairs that can be derived from the band combination where UL Tx switching Rel-18 is supported.\n\nIf the UE implements the CR and the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue, there is no inter-operability issue since it is expected that \"possible band pairs\" should be interpreted as all the band pairs that can be derived from the band combination where UL Tx switching Rel-18 is supported." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509102> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change “RRCReconfiguration message including reconfigurationWithSync was received” to “RRCReconfiguration message including reconfigurationWithSync was applied” in the procedure description of logging nrPreviousCell in RLF report.\n\nImpact analysis\nArchitecture options\nStandalone\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRLF report\n\nInter-operability:\nThere is no Inter-operability impact if this CR is only implemented by UE or network." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509103> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change “RRCReconfiguration message including reconfigurationWithSync was received” to “RRCReconfiguration message including reconfigurationWithSync was applied” in the procedure description of logging nrPreviousCell in RLF report.\n\nImpact analysis\nArchitecture options\nStandalone\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRLF report\n\nInter-operability:\nThere is no Inter-operability impact if this CR is only implemented by UE or network." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509118> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Stage 2 description for logged MDT is corrected to capture that upon UE failing to re-select to a suitable cell that supports the NSAG ID with the highest priority and selecting to a different cell, following information are logged in logged MDT report:\n-\tThe NSAG ID with the highest priority;\n-\tCell ID of the re-selected cell;" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509121> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In field description for groupBasedBeamReporting, add following restriction: \"The network configures groupBasedBeamReporting-v1800 only if groupBasedBeamReporting-v1710 is configured.\"\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture option: NR SA, NR-DC, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC.\nImpacted functionality: Group-based beam reporting.\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, network might configure groupBasedBeamReporting-v1800 without groupBasedBeamReporting-v1710 in a CSI-ReportConfig, which the UE could consider to be invalid." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509122> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In field description for groupBasedBeamReporting, add following restriction: \"The network configures groupBasedBeamReporting-v1800 only if groupBasedBeamReporting-v1710 is configured.\"\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture option: NR SA, NR-DC, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC.\nImpacted functionality: Group-based beam reporting.\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, network might configure groupBasedBeamReporting-v1800 without groupBasedBeamReporting-v1710 in a CSI-ReportConfig, which the UE could consider to be invalid." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509125> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1) reword maxNumberJointTCI-AcrossCells-r18 so make it clear that it applies to activated joint TCI states in the band, including joint LTM TCI states of all candidate cells in the band and joint TCI states of all serving cells in the band\n2) add missing \"in the band\" for maxNumberDL-TCI-AcrossCells-r18 and reword it to make it clear that it applies to activated DL TCI states in the band, including DL LTM TCI states of all candidates cells in the band and DL TCI states of all serving cells in the band\n3) reword maxNumberUL-TCI-AcrossCells-r18 to make it clear that it applies to activated UL TCI states in the band, including UL LTM TCI states of all candidates cells in the band and UL TCI states of all serving cells in the band\n4) for maxNumberCells-r18, change \"maximum number of configured cells for joint candidate cells for joint (or separate DL/UL) LTM TCI state(s)\" to \"maximum number of candidate cells with joint (or separate DL/UL) LTM TCI state(s)\".\n5) Remove \"DL\" after \"joint\" and remove \"separate\" before \"UL\" and before \"DL\".\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nLTM TCI state activation\n\nInter-operability:\nIt the network implements the CR but not the UE, or vice-versa, the network and the UE may count activated TCI states for LTM differently, which may result in exceeding the UE capability and unpredictable UE behaviour (possibly, the Ue may perform re-establishment)." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509126> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1) reword maxNumberJointTCI-AcrossCells-r18 so make it clear that it applies to activated joint TCI states in the band, including joint LTM TCI states of all candidate cells in the band and joint TCI states of all serving cells in the band\n2) add missing \"in the band\" of maxNumberDL-TCI-AcrossCells-r18 and reword it to make it clear that it applies to activated DL TCI states in the band, including DL LTM TCI states of all candidates cells in the band and DL TCI states of all serving cells in the band\n3) reword maxNumberUL-TCI-AcrossCells-r18 to make it clear that it applies to activated UL TCI states in the band, including UL LTM TCI states of all candidates cells in the band and UL TCI states of all serving cells in the band\n4) for maxNumberCells-r18, change \"maximum number of configured cells for joint candidate cells for joint (or separate DL/UL) LTM TCI state(s)\" to \"maximum number of candidate cells with joint (or separate DL/UL) LTM TCI state(s)\".\n5) Remove \"DL\" after \"joint\" and remove \"separate\" before \"UL\" and before \"DL\".\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nLTM TCI state activation\n\nInter-operability:\nIt the network implements the CR but not the UE, or vice-versa, the network and the UE may count activated TCI states for LTM differently, which may result in exceeding the UE capability and unpredictable UE behaviour (possibly, the Ue may perform re-establishment)." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509129> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Replace measIdleValidityDuration with measReselectionValidityDuration  in 5.7.10.3 so that the UE sets the validityStatus properly for NR reselection measurement reporting.\n\nAdd a new field validityStatus-r18 within the IE MeasResultsPerCellIdleEUTRA to allow UE to set validityStatus for reporting valid E-UTRA measurement results.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, NE-DC, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nValidation of reported idle/inactive and reselection measurements\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue but network has no idea how UE checked the reported measurement validity and might configure CA/DC wrongly.\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509131> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the additionalSpectrumEmission for each SL positioning frequencies broadcasted in SIB23;\nAdd the additionalSpectrumEmission for each SL positioning frequencies indicated in SL-PreconfigurationNR.\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nSA\nImpacted functionality:\nSL positioning\nInter-operability:\nIf UE implements the CR and NW does not\nthere is no inter-operability issue but UE will never get the additionalSpectrumEmission from gNB\nIf NW implements the CR and UE does not\nthere is no inter-operability issue but UE cannot read the additionalSpectrumEmission provided by the gNB" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509132> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the additionalSpectrumEmission for each SL positioning frequencies broadcasted in SIB23;\nAdd the additionalSpectrumEmission for each SL positioning frequencies indicated in SL-PreconfigurationNR.\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nSA\nImpacted functionality:\nSL positioning\nInter-operability:\nIf UE implements the CR and NW does not\nthere is no inter-operability issue but UE will never get the additionalSpectrumEmission from gNB\nIf NW implements the CR and UE does not\nthere is no inter-operability issue but UE cannot read the additionalSpectrumEmission provided by the gNB" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509133> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Updated the conditional presence to specify that PDCP configuration is always provided when SRB4 or SRB5 is setup.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nQoE\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA, NR-DC\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not,\nthere is no issue.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, then the SRB4/SRB5 addition may fail as the UE can not handle the SRB4/SRB5 configuration without PDCP config." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509134> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1. Update procedure text that UE supporting CPAC MRO also sets timeSCGFailure/ previousPSCellId / failedPSCellId in SCGFailureInformation, and align the terminology used in 38.306\n2. Update the field description of previousPSCellId and failedPSCellId to indicate it is also for CPAC.\n3. simplify field description of firstTriggeredEvent to ‘The field is to indicate the first fulfilled conditional execution condition’ and remove the ‘included in choConfig’ in the field description of timeBetweenEvents.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted Architecture options:\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nCPAC MRO\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE may not report timeSCGFailure, failedPSCellId and previousPSCellId in SCGFailureInformation which leads to wrong UE implementation and impossible to detect CPAC MRO at NW’s side.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509135> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1. Update procedure text that UE supporting CPAC MRO also sets timeSCGFailure/ previousPSCellId / failedPSCellId in SCGFailureInformation, and align the terminology used in 38.306\n2. Update the field description of previousPSCellId and failedPSCellId to indicate it is also for CPAC.\n3. simplify field description of firstTriggeredEvent to ‘The field is to indicate the first fulfilled conditional execution condition’ and remove the ‘included in choConfig’ in the field description of timeBetweenEvents.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted Architecture options:\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nCPAC MRO\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE may not report timeSCGFailure, failedPSCellId and previousPSCellId in SCGFailureInformation which leads to wrong UE implementation and impossible to detect CPAC MRO at NW’s side.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509142> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change subcarrierSpacing values for FR1 in IE SCS-SpecificCarrier from \"15 or 30kHz\" to \"15, 30 or 60kHz\".\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR standalone, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\nImpacted functionality:\nsubcarrierSpacing configurations\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to this CR while the UE is not, there might be inter-operability issues because the network may configure a subcarrierSpacing value not supported by the UE.\nIf the UE is implemented according to this CR while the network is not, there are no inter-operability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509162> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the restriction that F field is set to 0 if the size of the MAC SDU is less than 256 bytes, otherwise it is set to 1.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSL-SCH data transfer\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the Tx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Rx UE is not, there is no interoperability issue.\nIf the Rx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Tx UE is not, the Rx UE may not be able to decode sidelink MAC subPDU properly.\nThere is no impact on the network.\n\nThis CR is mandatory to implement for UEs supporting SL-SCH data transfer." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509164> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the restriction that F field is set to 0 if the size of the MAC SDU or variable-sized MAC control element is less than 256 bytes, otherwise it is set to 1.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSL-SCH data transfer\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the Tx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Rx UE is not, there is no interoperability issue.\nIf the Rx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Tx UE is not, the Rx UE may not be able to decode sidelink MAC subPDU properly.\nThere is no impact on the network.\n\nThis CR is mandatory to implement for UEs supporting SL-SCH data transfer." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509165> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the restriction that F field is set to 0 if the size of the MAC SDU or variable-sized MAC control element is less than 256 bytes, otherwise it is set to 1.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSL-SCH data transfer\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the Tx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Rx UE is not, there is no interoperability issue.\nIf the Rx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Tx UE is not, the Rx UE may not be able to decode sidelink MAC subPDU properly.\nThere is no impact on the network.\n\nThis CR is mandatory to implement for UEs supporting SL-SCH data transfer." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509169> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the restriction that F field is set to 0 if the size of the MAC SDU or variable-sized MAC control element is less than 256 bytes, otherwise it is set to 1.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSL-SCH data transfer\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the Tx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Rx UE is not, there is no interoperability issue.\nIf the Rx UE is implemented according to the CR and the Tx UE is not, the Rx UE may not be able to decode sidelink MAC subPDU properly.\nThere is no impact on the network.\n\nThis CR is mandatory to implement for UEs supporting SL-SCH data transfer." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509171> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “The UE is allowed to indicate this capability for the band combination with more than 2 intra-band NR CCs, but this capability is only applicable for the corresponding fallback band combination with only 2 intra-band NR CCs.” to the field description of the intraBandNR-CA-non-collocated-r18;\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR CA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nType 2 requirement for the non-collocated CA\n\nInter-operability:\n\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the network may misunderstand these capabilities if there are reported with parent BC.\n\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE is unable to indicate these capabilities with the parent BC, which may lead to signalling overhead." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509172> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Include the above agreement to the field descriptions of the\nintraBandNR-CA-non-collocated-r18/ intraBandNR-CA-non-collocated-r19/ interBandMRDC-WithOverlapDL-Bands-r19 as following:\n\n1: Add “The UE is allowed to indicate this capability for the band combination with more than 2 intra-band NR CCs, but this capability is only applicable for the corresponding fallback band combination with only 2 intra-band NR CCs.” to the field description of the intraBandNR-CA-non-collocated-r18/ intraBandNR-CA-non-collocated-r19;\n\n2: Add “The UE is allowed to indicate this capability for the band combination with more than 1 NR CC on the corresponding NR band (i.e. the NR band that overlaps with EUTRA band), but this capability is only applicable to the fallback band combination with only single CC on that NR band.” to the field description of the interBandMRDC-WithOverlapDL-Bands-r19.\n\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR CA, EN-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nType 2 and Type 4 requirements for the non-collocated CA and EN-DC\n\nInter-operability:\n\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the network may misunderstand these capabilities for the parent BC.\n\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE is unable to indicate these capabilities if they are reported with parent BC, which may lead to signalling overhead." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509179> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "For CFRA, RO type selection/indication via dedicated RRC signalling or MAC CE is added.\nFor CBRA, RO type selection for initial PRACH transmissions is added.\nMiscellaneous corrections on SBFD RACH configuration option.\nRemove “in case of SBFD operation” from the sentence “Two types of UE-to-UE CLI reporting are supported in case of SBFD operation: L1-based reporting and L3-based reporting.”" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509183> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Disaster broadcast information and access barring parameters for disaster roaming in EPS are added in SIB30.\nAccess barring check procedure are updated to support access control for disaster roaming access.\nInformative timer table is updated to include a new timer related to disaster roaming access." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509191> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1-1. Add a new redirection information element that includes the NB-IoT carrier frequency related information and a list of satellite IDs.\n1-2. Fix the suffix for carrierFreq in CarrierInfoEUTRA-r19 in RRCConnectionRelease.\n2. Fix the suffix for carrierFreq in RedirectedCarrierInfo-NB-v1900 in RRCConnectionRelease-NB.\n3. Add a new capability signalling ntn-Redirection-NB-r19 in Other-Parameters-v1900, indicating whether the UE supports redirection from an E-UTRAN terrestrial network to an NB-IoT non-terrestrial network." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509195> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1) In the field description of ta-Report, clarify that the UE may include TA report during transmission using PUR.\n2) For specific parameters such as additionalSpectrumEmission and p-Max, a reference to TS 36.102/36.108 is included into their respective field descriptions.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nIoT NTN\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\tIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, no inter-operability issues are foreseen.\n2.\tIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, no inter-operability issues are foreseen." .
