<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509223> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In 5.8.9.7.2, added the sentence to describe L2 U2N relay UE only initiate PC5 relay RLC channel addition towards a remote UE if the remote UE is indicated to use this RLC channel in accordance with sl-SRAP-ConfigRelay.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality\nLayer 2 Sidelink UE-to-NW Relay\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf one UE implements the CR but not the other UE, there is no inter-operability issue.\nImplementation of this CR from Rel-17 will not cause interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509224> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Capture the missing format of sl-MeasResultsCandRelay-r18 in IndirectPathFailureInformation.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality\nNR SL Multi-path relay\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf one UE implements the CR but not the other UE, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509225> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Capture the missing format of sl-MeasResultsCandRelay-r18 in IndirectPathFailureInformation.\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality\nNR SL Multi-path relay\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implements the CR but not the network, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the network implements the CR but not the UE, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf one UE implements the CR but not the other UE, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509226> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Dummy the Rel-18 UE capability of supporting UL time window for RedCap UE positioning SRS frequency hopping in LPP specification\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nSA\nImpacted functionality:\nRedCap UE positioning SRS frequency hopping\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE is implemented according to this CR while the NW is not, there is no inter-operability issue;\nIf the NW is implemented according to this CR while the UE is not, LMF may receive the UE capability that it does not understand/support." .
