<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509243> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In 5.2.3.1.1, update the specification to preclude the case on “not consider the corresponding RLC SDU for transmission”.\nIn 5.2.3.2.5, clarify that RX_Highest_Status falls outside of the receiving window, RX_Highest_Status is updated to RX_Next.\nIn 5.3.3.3, the NOTE is updated as below:\nNOTE: If stopRetxDiscardedSDU is configured, when all RLC SDUs with SNs up to and including POLL_SN have been positively acknowledged or indicated as discarded from upper layer (e.g., PDCP), the transmitting side of an AM RLC entity may stop and reset the running t-PollRetransmit.\nIn 5.3.4, update the NOTE 3 to include the update for RX_Highest_Status.\nIn 7.1, the definition of RX_Next is updated as:\na) RX_Next – Receive state variable\nThis state variable holds the value of the SN of the first RLC SDU not delivered to upper layers, but still wait for, and it serves as the lower edge of the receiving window. It is initially set to 0, and is updated whenever the AM RLC entity receives an RLC SDU with SN = RX_Next or t-RxDiscard expires." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509246> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the description in the DSR MAC CE that the MAC CE is variable-sized MAC CE\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted functionality:\nDelay status report MAC CE\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR but the UE is not; or if the UE is implemented accoridng to the CR while the network is not, there is no inter-operability issues since it could be inferred from the other parts of the MAC spec." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509256> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Remove “if available” in the procedure description of logging previousPSCellId in SCGFailureInformation for reconfiguration with sync failure case in 5.7.3.5 section.\nChange “PSCell addition failure” to “PSCell addition” in the field description of previousPSCellId.\nUpdated the concerned condition to specify that the logging previousPSCellId is performed only if the UE entered cell through PSCell change.\nMove the procedure description of timeSCGFailure outside the condition “3>\tif the last RRCReconfiguration message including the reconfigurationWithSync for the PSCell change was received to enter the PSCell in which the SCG failure was declared:” for RLF case in 5.7.3.5 section.\n\nImpact analysis\nArchitecture options\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSCGFailureInformation\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it is not clear how the UE logs previousPSCellId when SCG failure occurs in case of the UE entered the PSCell due to PSCell addition.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, then there are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509257> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Remove “if available” in the procedure description of logging previousPSCellId in SCGFailureInformation for reconfiguration with sync failure case in 5.7.3.5 section.\nChange “PSCell addition failure” to “PSCell addition” in the field description of previousPSCellId.\nUpdated the concerned condition to specify that the logging previousPSCellId is performed only if the UE entered cell through PSCell change.\nMove the procedure description of timeSCGFailure outside the condition “3>\tif the last RRCReconfiguration message including the reconfigurationWithSync for the PSCell change was received to enter the PSCell in which the SCG failure was declared:” for RLF case in 5.7.3.5 section.\n\nImpact analysis\nArchitecture options\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSCGFailureInformation\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it is not clear how the UE logs previousPSCellId when SCG failure occurs in case of the UE entered the PSCell due to PSCell addition.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, then there are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509258> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Remove “if available” in the procedure description of logging previousPSCellId in SCGFailureInformation for reconfiguration with sync failure case and radio link failure case in 5.7.3.5 section.\nChange “PSCell addition failure” to “PSCell addition” in the field description of previousPSCellId.\nUpdated the concerned condition to specify that the logging previousPSCellId is performed only if the UE entered cell through PSCell change.\nMove the procedure description of timeSCGFailure outside the condition “3>\tif the last RRCReconfiguration message including the reconfigurationWithSync for the PSCell change was received to enter the PSCell in which the SCG failure was declared:” for RLF case in 5.7.3.5 section.\n\nImpact analysis\nArchitecture options\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nSCGFailureInformation\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, it is not clear how the UE logs previousPSCellId when SCG failure occurs in case of the UE entered the PSCell due to PSCell addition.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, then there are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509261> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following agreed RILs are captured in this CR:\nC064, N001, H346, B001" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509262> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following RILs are agreed and captured in the CR:\nC051, C052,C053, C054, C056, C059, C061, C062, C063, X552, X553, H304, H306, H307, H308, H309, H311, H312, H313, N043, N044, N045, S018, S019, S022, S023, E016, E017, E018, E019, E020, E021, E022, E028, E046, E047, E048, J030, J031, J033, J034, Z301, Z302, Z303, Z304, Z306, Z309, Z310\n\nThe following RILs are also agreed during the online session at the meeting RAN2#131bis\nC058, E051, H310\n\nThe following new RILs added to the review file after the meeting RAN2#131bis are also captured and their status is changed to “propAgree” in the comment file.\nZ311, Z312, S059 and S060\n\nAfter the meeting RAN2#132, in addition to capturing the changes agreed from TDoc R2-2508259, the RIL Z305 is also captured in this CR." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509263> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The LTM cell switch is included in the MRO for successful HO\nIt is clarified that the LTM cell switch just applies to MCG\nIt is clarified when the UE determines that the RACH less LTM is successfully completed\nSome editorial issues are fixed" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509265> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "SSB-less SCell definition is added and definitions are removed from the field descriptions." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509266> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify that the “In case of an RedCap-specific initial downlink BWP that is associated with NCD-SSB, the SSB is the NCD-SSB. Otherwise, the SSB is the CD-SSB.” is only for SDT case. For RACH-less, to clarify that “in case of the downlink BWP indicated by firstActiveDownlinkBWP-Id that is associated with NCD-SSB, the SSB is the NCD-SSB; otherwise, the SSB is the CD-SSB.”\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G Architecture options:\nNR SA, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRACH-less handover, NCD-SSB\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implementes according to this CR but the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the network implements according to this CR but the UE does not, the UE may not expect the CG-based RACH-less HO configured to be mapped with NCD-SSB." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509267> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify that the “In case of an RedCap-specific initial downlink BWP that is associated with NCD-SSB, the SSB is the NCD-SSB. Otherwise, the SSB is the CD-SSB.” is only for SDT case. For RACH-less, to clarify that “in case of the downlink BWP indicated by firstActiveDownlinkBWP-Id that is associated with NCD-SSB, the SSB is the NCD-SSB; otherwise, the SSB is the CD-SSB.”\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G Architecture options:\nNR SA, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nRACH-less handover, NCD-SSB\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the UE implementes according to this CR but the network does not, there is no inter-operability issue.\nIf the network implements according to this CR but the UE does not, the UE may not expect the CG-based RACH-less HO configured to be mapped with NCD-SSB." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509302> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Adding stage 2 support for 5G Broadcast CAS Muting." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509304> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the following to the Definitions clause:\n\nIAB-MT: As defined in TS 38.300 [2]. A mobile IAB-MT uses the same procedures and behaviours (including Cell Reservations and Access Restrictions) specified for the IAB-MT, unless explicitly stated otherwise.\n\n\nImpact Analysis\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA\n\nImpacted functionality: (m)IAB\n\nInter-operability:\n\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the mIAB-MT is not, there is no inter-operability issue.\n\n2.\t If the mIAB-MT is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509305> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the following to the Definitions clause:\n\nIAB-MT: As defined in TS 38.300 [2]. A mobile IAB-MT uses the same procedures and behaviours (including Cell Reservations and Access Restrictions) specified for the IAB-MT, unless explicitly stated otherwise.\n\n\nImpact Analysis\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA\n\nImpacted functionality: (m)IAB\n\nInter-operability:\n\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the mIAB-MT is not, there is no inter-operability issue.\n\n2.\t If the mIAB-MT is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509309> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following functionality to support early CSI acquisition for handover is added\nearly CSI acquisition configuration to ReconfigurationWithSync\nper band optional UE capability to indicate support of CSI-RS and CSI-IM measurement and CSI reporting\nper band optional UE capability to indicate support of CSI-RS measurement and CSI reporting without CSI-IM resource configuration" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509310> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following two capabilities are introduced:\nOptional per band UE capability to indicate whether the UE supports early CSI-RS and CSI-IM measurement and CSI reporting\nOptional per band UE capability to indicate whether the UE supports early CSI-RS measurement and CSI reporting without CSI-IM resource configuration" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509314> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In 5.3.5.18.6, delete the text related to fast recovery case upon SCG LTM execution.\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nLTM\n\nInter-operability:\nIf NW implements this CR but UE not, there is no inter-operatibility issue found;\nIf UE implements this CR but NW not, there is no inter-operatibility issue found.\n." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509315> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 4.2.7.2\n- Clarified that “In each FR, the UE shall set this capability consistently for all bands for which it indicates support of ltm-MCG-IntraFreq-r18, and for all bands for which it indicates support of ltm-SCG-IntraFreq-r18” for the capabilities ltm-BeamIndicationJointTCI-r18, ltm-BeamIndicationSeparateTCI-r18, ltm-MAC-CE-JointTCI-r18, and ltm-MAC-CE-SeparateTCI-r18.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: SA and NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality: LTM capabilities\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the network needs extra mechanisms to handled discrepancies in UE capabilities across bands that are not expected to exist in UE implementations.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the network needs extra mechanisms to handled discrepancies in UE capabilities across bands that are not expected to exist in UE implementations." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509316> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 4.2.7.2\n- Clarified that “In each FR, the UE shall set this capability consistently for all bands for which it indicates support of ltm-MCG-IntraFreq-r18, and for all bands for which it indicates support of ltm-SCG-IntraFreq-r18” for the capabilities ltm-BeamIndicationJointTCI-r18, ltm-BeamIndicationSeparateTCI-r18, ltm-MAC-CE-JointTCI-r18, and ltm-MAC-CE-SeparateTCI-r18, ltm-BeamIndicationJointTCI-CSI-RS-r19, ltm-BeamIndicationSeparateTCI-CSI-RS-r19, ltm-MAC-CE-JointTCI-CSI-RS-r19, ltm-MAC-CE-SeparateTCI-CSI-RS-r19.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: SA and NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality: LTM capabilities\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the network needs extra mechanisms to handled discrepancies in UE capabilities across bands that are not expected to exist in UE implementations.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the network needs extra mechanisms to handled discrepancies in UE capabilities across bands that are not expected to exist in UE implementations." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509320> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Updated description of the capability ltm-MCG-NRDC-Release-r18 to explain that if the UE also indicates the support of ltm-Recovery-r18, then this capability also indicates the UE supports LTM for MCG with the release of NR-DC configuration as part of LTM recovery procedure.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nNR-DC configuration handling during MCG LTM\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the network may assume the UE supports NR-DC configuration release during LTM recovery when in fact the UE cannot, which results in a configuration mismatch.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue, but the options of candidate configurations provided by network may be limited." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509321> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Updated description of the capability ltm-MCG-NRDC-Release-r18 to explain that if the UE also indicates the support of ltm-Recovery-r18, then this capability also indicates the UE supports LTM for MCG with the release of NR-DC configuration as part of LTM recovery procedure.\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nNRDC configuartion during MCG LTM\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the network may assume the UE supports NR-DC configuration release during LTM recovery when in fact the UE cannot, which results in a configuration mismatch.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue, but the options of candidate configurations provided by network may be limited." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509322> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 5.3.5.13.7\n- Corrected parameter name from sk-CounterConfigToRemoveList to sk-CounterConfigToReleaseList\n\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality: CPAC\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE may never release an sk-counter which the network wants to release.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509323> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 5.3.5.13.7\n- Corrected parameter name from sk-CounterConfigToRemoveList to sk-CounterConfigToReleaseList\n\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality: CPAC\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE may never release an sk-counter which the network wants to release.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509326> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "- Addition of a Note in 9.2.4 for gap determination in OD-SSB.\n- Align with the agreement that legacy MO is applied when OD-SSB and AO-SSB are in same frequency in 9.2.4.\n- Capturing that the UE can receive common DCI format 2_9 for SSB adaptation for a deactivated SCell but the UE shall ignore it for the deactivated SCell.\n- Removal of “deactivation” in the sentence regarding OD-SSB transmission command." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509327> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "if CE is applicable for random access procedure and RACH-ConfigCommon associated with selected random access resource set includes additional RO, UE does not use additional RO configured in this RACH-ConfigCommon\nAll UEs (including (e)RedCap UEs) perform an OD-SIB1 request and monitoring the same way. The UE monitors PDCCH based on configuration in OD-SIB1 configuration for OD-SIB1 recpetion.\nthat f_id for the additional PRACH resources is reinterpreted as the index of the PRACH occasion in the frequency domain plus the number of FDMed legacy ROs\nAddition of adap-ssbPeriodicityIndication-RNTI to the list of monitored RNTIs during the active time of C-DRX\nChange of some RRC parameter names to match updated names in TS 38.331" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509329> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The corrections associated with the RILs below are captured:\n\nX204, X205, C182, N002, H126, H100, H101, H102, J003, J004, V501, L203, L204, L205, L206, L209, L210, N003, S030, S031, S035, Z103, A101, A102, H129, V500, C181, S061, Z104, Z106, V504, V505, S062, S063, F001, O009\n\nThe names of some ASN.1 fields are corrected with respect to the RRC naming rules (editorial)." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509333> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Updated description in clause 5.18.36 to clarify that deactivation upon reconfiguration occurs at the candidate cell level; specifically, UE shall deactivate all TCI states of an LTM candidate cell upon (re)configuration of any TCI state of the LTM candidate cell.\nUpdated description in clause 5.18.36 to clarify that UE deactivate all candidate TCI state upon non-LTM mobility;\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nCandidate TCI state deactivation upon reconfiguration and mobility\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE may misinterpret the signalling scope from the network. This could result in a mismatch in candidate TCI activation status and unnecessary deactivation of additional candidate TCI states.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the network may incorrectly indicate the scope of deactivation. This could result in a mismatch in candidate TCI activation status and failure to properly deactivate certain TCI states." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509334> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Updated description in clause 5.18.36 to clarify that deactivation upon reconfiguration occurs at the candidate cell level; specifically, UE shall deactivate all TCI states of an LTM candidate cell upon (re)configuration of any TCI state of the LTM candidate cell.\nUpdated description in clause 5.18.36 to clarify that UE deactivate all candidate TCI state upon non-LTM mobility;\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality:\nCandidate TCI state deactivation upon reconfiguration and mobility\n\nInter-operability:\nIf the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, the UE may misinterpret the signalling scope from the network. This could result in a mismatch in candidate TCI activation status and unnecessary deactivation of additional candidate TCI states.\nIf the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, the network may incorrectly indicate the scope of deactivation. This could result in a mismatch in candidate TCI activation status and failure to properly deactivate certain TCI states." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509336> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Align some RRC paramters to RRC specification.\nClarify that the SR resource for (truncated) MR MAC CE has the same priority as the SR resource for BFR MAC CE:\nIf the SR resource for (truncated) MR MAC CE overlaps with SR resource for BFR MAC CE (for an SCell or a BFD-RS set), it’s up to UE implementation which SR resource to be selected. Update the Note in the current MAC specification.\nClarify the behaviour of the UE when there is an overlap of PUCCH resources for pending SR between the different possible combinations.\nClarify that if an ltm-CSI-ReportConfig or an ltm-CSI-ResourceConfig associated with that ltm-CSI-ReportConfig is modified or removed, RRC layer should trigger MAC layer to remove the measurement reporting entry, stop the periodical reporting timer, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this ltm-CSI-ReportConfigId.\nClarity that if an ltm-CSI-ReportConfig or an ltm-CSI-ResourceConfig associated with that ltm-CSI-ReportConfig is removed from or modified in the current UE configuration, the MAC entity shall cancel the triggered L1 measurement report associated with the ltm-CSI-ReportConfig.\nClarify that the UE releases the stored TA value and stops the corresponding CLTM TAT if the NW releases the execution condition for the LTM candidate cell.\nUpdate “i.e. the RS configured in the indicated TCI State of the SpCell,” to include both SSB and CSI-RS in the procedure and the description of serving RS for Event LTM2/3/5.\nReplace ‘SSBRI or CRI’ with ‘RS resource index’ in clause 5.35.3.1 so that managing RS resource index for the serving beam can be left up to UE implementation.\nThe condition\n1> for each ltm-CSI-ReportConfigId included in the LTM-CSI-ReportConfig:\nis changed as:\n1> for each ltm-CSI-ReportConfigId included in the SpCell for L1 measurement and event-triggered report:\nRemove the duplicated description for SR in 5.35.4\nAdd the case that “UE can only perform RACH-based LTM for CLTM recovery” in the specification.\nClarify that upon release of the CLTM execution condition, the UE stops CLTM TAT if running even if the corresponding LTM candidate configuration is kept.\nClarify that for beam selection for L3-based RACH-less CLTM based on a configured threshold, the existing cg-RRC-RSRP-ThresholdSSB is re-used.\nClarify that the deactivation of SP CSI-RS for L1-RSRP from the target cell after reconfiguration with sync.\nReplacing “A/D” to “IM” in Octet 2 for the explicit indication of the presence of CSI Resource Configuration ID2 in clause 6.1.3.12a.\nClarify that the CSI Resource Configuration ID2 is only used to indicate the CSI-IM resource set, i.e. remove “CSI-RS and” from the sentence “SP CSI-RS and CSI-IM resource set for the candidate cell(s) associated with the CSI Resource Configuration ID2 in the same octet”.\nClarify that the TCI-state indicated in the SP CSI-RS/CSI-IM Resource Set Activation/Deactivation for Candidate Cell MAC CE refers to TCI-state provided in the IE LTM-TCI-Info.\nSome editorial changes and typo have been fixed." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509337> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Following changes are done and following issues are fixed:\n- Upon inter-CU MCG LTM execution, SN key update is also needed for the case that SN terminated bearer configured with MCG RLC leg only\n- Wrong removal of report configuration associated with L3 based CLTM upon reconfiguration with sync\n- Clarified whether the UE should stop the LTM conditions evaluation based on L1 measurements and/or based on L3 measurements\n- Avoid stop CLTM evaluation for new configured CLTM conditions\n- Clarified that UE should stop the corresponding LTM conditions evaluation before release the ltm-ServingCellExecutionCondition\n- Correction on conditional LTM cell switch execution for only one triggered LTM candidate configuration\n- Clarification on the sk-counter contained in the ltm-CandidateConfig for SCG LTM\n- Corrected wrong IE name\n- Added new RAN1 paramenters according to R1-2506622\n\nAdditional changes from what have been agreed in RAN2#131bis are the following:\n- It is clarified in the procedural text that, upon the execution of an LTM cell switch procedure with security key change, the UE releases all RLC bearers (configurations and bearers itself).\n- The field ltm-CSI-ReportConfig-r19 within LTM-Candidate IE is changed to SetupRelease\n- Created a new UE variable to store the execution conditions and procedural text has been modified accordingly\n- Clarified in field description that ltm-CSI-ReportConfig can only be configured within ServingCellConfig of the SpCell\n- Added UE handling for the case when UE keeps two VarLTM-ServingCellNoSecurityChange\n- The network does not set mrdc-ReleaseAndAdd for MCG LTM with SCG configuration, and the UE autonomously release the SCG part of the current UE configuration upon LTM cell switch execution, i.e. follow the same actions as LTM cell switch triggered on the SCG\n- The fields ltm-ReferenceConfigurationSCG, ltm-Config, ltm-ReferenceConfigurationMCG are added the exception list in section 11.2.3 of TS 38.331\n- Clarified for beam selection for L3-based RACH-less CLTM based on a configured threshold, the existing cg-RRC-RSRP-ThresholdSSB is re-used\n- Clarification on ltm-ServingCellExecutionCondition set to release\n- PDCP data recovery should not be performed for all the AM DRBs which is part of the current UE configuration\n- Clarification on stopping LTM cell switch conditions evaluation in LTM cell switch execution conditions modification procedure\n- Corrections fields for event triggered reports but not to execution conditions.\n- Updated list of parameters to be exchanged between MN and SN withing the inter-node RRC messages" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509339> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 4.2.7.5\n- Clarified for the capability pdcch-RACH-PrepTime-TargetBandList-r18 that for the case where the PRACH bandwidth of target band is inside of the configured UL BWP, the capability is not applicable and the value of RF/BB preparation time is zero.\n- Clarified for the capability pdcch-RACH-Switching-TargetBandTimeList-r18 that for the case where the PRACH bandwidth of target band is inside of the configured UL BWP, this capability is not applicable, and the interruption length (Y ms) due to RF re-tuning is zero.\n\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality: LTM\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509340> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 4.2.7.5\n- Clarified for the capability pdcch-RACH-PrepTime-TargetBandList-r18 that for the case where the PRACH bandwidth of target band is inside of the configured UL BWP, the capability is not applicable and the value of RF/BB preparation time is zero.\n- Clarified for the capability pdcch-RACH-Switching-TargetBandTimeList-r18 that For the case where the PRACH bandwidth of target band is inside of the configured UL BWP, this capability is not applicable, and the interruption length (Y ms) due to RF re-tuning is zero.\n\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality: LTM\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t If the network is implemented according to the CR and the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue.\n\n2.\t If the UE is implemented according to the CR and the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509350> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Update the description of the capability related to time interleaving by adding “up to a maximum TBS”.\nIntroduce a new capability as following related to the cyclic shift for PMCH: pmch-CyclicShiftAlpha3-r19\nEditorial changes" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509353> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In 5.5.4.24, corrected a typo in Event A3H2 inequality (“A3H1-4” to “A3H2-4”).\nIn IE SL-CBR-CommonTxDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-List, deleted redundant “-“ in sl-PRS-MaxNum-Transmissions, to align with RRC naming convention, and with name used in MAC spec (TS 38.321).\n\nImpact Analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options: NR SA, (NG)EN-DC, NE-DC,NR-DC\n\nImpacted functionality: Miscellaneous\n\nInter-operability:\nThere are no interoperability issues." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509354> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In 5.5.4.24, corrected a typo in Event A3H2 inequality (“A3H1-4” to “A3H2-4”).\nIn 6.3.5, IE SL-CBR-CommonTxDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-List, deleted redundant “-“ in sl-PRS-MaxNum-Transmissions, to align with RRC naming convention, and with name used in MAC spec (TS 38.321).\nIn IE CSI-ReportConfig, deleted duplicated field description text for reportQuantity.\nIn IEs CSI-ReportConfig, CodebookParameters, FeatureSetUplink, FeatureSetUplinkPerCC and MIMO-ParametersPerBand, some non-ASCII characters are replaced. Non-ASCII characters in RRC ASN.1 (also in ASN.1 comments) are avoided, not to cause problems with certain ASN.1 compilers.\nIn 5.3.7.3, indicated text should have black font colour.\nIn 5.3.7.3, added a missing new line." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509355> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a supported NB band list into the UE-EUTRA-Capability-v1900." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509358> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The repetition of PDCCH in common search space introduced in Rel-19 NR NTN WI is also applicable for TN for FR1 only\nAdd in section 19 “Support for NR NTN coverage enhancements” the description of the repetition of PDCCH in common search space for FR1 TN." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509361> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Introduction of a new inter-RAT parameter to indicate the supported NB-IoT NTN bands." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509363> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Introduction of NR-NTN satellite information into SystemInformationBlockType33-NB (similarly to what was done to enable LTE to NR-NTN mobility), removal restriction in SystemInformationBlockType33 on indicating neighSatelliteInfoListNR only in TN cell, introduction of NR-NTN carrier frequency and satellite information into SystemInformationBlockType27-NB and SystemInformationBlockType27." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509366> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following corrections from the agreed RIL [S905] are implemented:\n\n[S905]: Change description of satAssistanceInfoList as:\n“List of satellite ID(s), used to associate with the satellite assistance information for neighbour cell measurements on this frequency for the purpose of redirection. Each satellite ID included in this list corresponds to a satelliteId configured in neighSatelliteInfoListNR within nr-r19 or neighSatelliteInfoList within eutra-NTN-r19 via SystemInformationBlockType33.”\n\nThe corrections from the agreed RIL [Z006] are implemented.\n\nThe following corrections from the agreed RIL [V230] are implemented:\nIf the SMTC is configured in the RRCConnectionRelease message, the offset is based on the assumption that the UE’s propagation delay difference between serving cell and neighbour cell equals to 0ms, and UE can adjust the SMTC offset based on the actual propagation delay (V230 is Agreed)\n\nnr-r19 is changed to nr-NTN-r19.\n\nFor subcarrierSpacingSSB-r19, remove the 120kHz and 240kHz from the candidate value.\n\nFor the smtc in RRCConnectionRelease, clarify that the UE assume the propagation delay difference between UE-serving cell at eNB and UE-neighbour cells at gNB equals to 0 ms, and UE can adjust the offset based on the actual propagation delay.\n\nFor the measTimingConfig in SIB24, clarify that the UE assume the the propagation delay difference between UE-serving cell at eNB and UE-neighbour cells at gNB equals to 0 ms, and UE can adjust the offset based on the actual propagation delay." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509367> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "This CR captures the corrections from the following agreed RILs based on the agreements made in RAN2#131bis and RAN2#132, and the RIL status in R2-2508274:\nV211, V212, N011, N013, V216, W801, C001, S901, S902, Z001, Z002, S907, Z004, Q002, V215." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509368> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "This CR captures the corrections from the following agreed RILs based on the agreement in RAN2#131bis and RAN2#132, and the RIL status in R2-2508277:\nV220, V221, Z051, Z052, Z053, Z054, N021, X501, Z055, H601, H600, N022" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509369> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “when explicit epoch time is present” for neighbor cell in the Epoch time field description.\n\n\nImpact analysis:\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nNeighbor satellite measurements\n\nInter-operability:\nIf UE implements this CR but network does not or vice versa, there may be\ndifferent understanding on the use of epoch time from serving cell when\nneighbor cell epoch time is absent in SIB19." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509370> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “when explicit epoch time is present” for neighbor cell in the Epoch time field description.\n\n\nImpact analysis:\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nNeighbor satellite measurements\n\nInter-operability:\nIf UE implements this CR but network does not or vice versa, there may be\ndifferent understanding on the use of epoch time from serving cell when\nneighbor cell epoch time is absent in SIB19." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509371> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “when explicit epoch time is present” for neighbor cell in the Epoch time field description.\n\n\nImpact analysis:\n\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nNR SA\n\nImpacted functionality:\nNeighbor satellite measurements\n\nInter-operability:\nIf UE implements this CR but network does not or vice versa, there may be\ndifferent understanding on the use of epoch time from serving cell when\nneighbor cell epoch time is absent in SIB19." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509372> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Added in clause 5.1A.2 “for IoT NTN TDD mode, if the subframe of the CB-Msg3 transmission is not a valid uplink subframe, it shall be postponed to the nearest uplink subframe”.\n\nUpdated Note 4 in clause 5.7 to cover IoT NTT TDD mode." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509375> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The corrections to the issues listed in R2-2507648 adressed by this CR are:\nThe description of the cell re-selection frequency prioritization for the UE capable of MBS Broadcast with ISA(s)\nThe description of the related enhancements for measurements in Downlink Coverage enhancements (i.e. 2 SMTC periodicities, 7 SMTC offsets and N closest location report)\nAnd editorial correction in clause 16.14.1." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509376> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Definition of UE capability to support the assistance information for inter-RAT cell selection from IoT NTN to NR NTN" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509377> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Definition of UE capability to support the assistance information for inter-RAT cell selection from NR NTN to IoT NTN" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509378> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In clause 4.2.9, introduce a new UE capability eventD2-MultiReferenceLocations-r19 to indicate whether the UE supports the configuration of multiple event D2 associated to different moving reference locations provided in the same measurement object as specified in TS 38.331 [9]. A UE supporting this feature shall also indicate support of eventD2-MeasReportTrigger-r18.\n\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nStandalone\nImpacted functionality:\nNR-NTN, Measurement\n\nInter-operability:\n\nIf the network supports the change and the UE does not, it is not possible for UE to map the different reference locations with multiple eventD2 and to report subsequent measurement result fulfills eventD2 entering/leaving condition.\nIf the UE supports the change and the network does not, there is no interoperability issue." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509379> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Section 5.2.8a is modified to exclude Inter-RAT cell search for acceptable cell." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509380> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "<1> Move the CB-RNTI derivation description from “clause 5.1a.3 CB-Msg4” reception to “clause 5.1a.2 CB-Msg3 transmission”; and in “Table 7.1-2: RNTI usage”, define CB-RNTI is used for CB-Msg3 transmission.\n<2> In 5.1a.3, determinate which MPDCCH narrowband is used for CB-Msg4 monitoring.\n<3> The condition for triggering the Msg3 DCQR is updated to include CB-Msg3-EDT case.\n\n<4> The back off index 0 to 12 indicates a back off parameter value of {0, 2, 4, 8, 10, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 36, 40} multiples of the CB-Msg3-transmission window periodicity. The back off indexes 13 to 15 are reserved for future usage.\n\n<5> Clarify that for CB-Msg3-EDT, the UE can perform uplink transmission without the timeAlignmentTimer running\n\n<6> To align the terminology, use \"MAC CMR\" instead of just “CMR”. Replace the confusing terminology \"CMR reception successful\" with “Contention Resolution successful\".\n\n<7> Clarify in clause 5.4.1 on the usage of CB-Msg3 grants for UL-SCH transmission.\n\n<8> Editorial changes and wording refinement." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509396> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Change additionalUplinkPowerControlToAddModList to uplink-PowerControlToAddModListExt and add the corresponding field description.\nCorrect the range value for sbfd-Config2-PUSCH-RB-Offset-r19.\nAdd references to other specifications.\nCorrect various editorial errors, improve various field descriptions.\nAdd restriction that rach-ConfigCommon and sbfd-RACH-DualConfig are configured in the same AdditionalRACH-Config when rach-ConfigCommon and sbfd-RACH-DualConfig are configured for the same FeatureCombination.\nMove ra-OccasionType-r19 to be within CFRA under RACH-ConfigDedicated.\nAdd the behavior description for parameters p0AlphaSetforPUSCH-SBFD, p0AlphaSetforPUCCH-SBFD, p0AlphaSetforSRS-SBFD      when the field alpha is absent.\nAdd the presence/absence restriction for parameters sbfd-RSRP-ThresholdMsg1-RepetitionNum2, sbfd-RSRP-ThresholdMsg1-RepetitionNum4, sbfd-RSRP-ThresholdMsg1-RepetitionNum8.\nFor list srs-RSRP-MeasResourceSetToReleaseList-r19, change the range constant to maxNrofSRS-RSRP-MeasResourceSets-r19.\nAdd the description on UE behavior regarding the mandatory field csi-RS-ResourceSetList in IE CSI-ResourceConfig when the field cli-MeasResourceSetList is configured.\nAdd \"Optional Need R\" for field resourcesForChannelCLI-r19." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509399> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1. In clause 6.2.1.1,\ntwo new agreed fields in A-IoT Paging message, i.e., Security Parameter Present Indication and Security Parameter are added;\n2. In clause 5.3.1.3,\n“or R2D Upper Layer Data Transfer message addressed to the device” is added as another condition of stopping msg2 reception;\n3. In clause 5.4.2:\nThe details for the two cases are added:\n“0 SDU & MDI =0” represents “no upper layer data available at all”. This covers all the cases where NAS doesn’t generate a NAS response.\n“0 SDU & MDI =1” represents “no upper layer data available due to delay NAS”.\n4. In clause 5.4.3:\nIt’s clarified that for CFA case, the inventory response may be also delayed so that the device may receive of an R2D Upper Layer Data Transfer message with Received Data Size field is set to 0 and set to 0 afterwards.\n5. In clause 6.2.1.1,\nPaging ID length is updated to 10 bits.\n6. In clause 6.2.1 and 6.2.2,\nfor each R2D message and D2R message, a length field and relevant value descriptions are added;\n7. In clause 6.1.1,\nsome general principles are summarized, including how to indicate optional field, how to interpret the real value of a codepoint, etc.;\n8. In clause 6.1.2,\nmessage type tables are moved to a new sub-clause;\n9. In other clauses,\nsome clarifications and corrections to some typos are made." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509400> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a Note to capture the logical connection between S1 Removal/Setup procedure and ephemeris info." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509401> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Specify the O&M requirements for the S&F mode indication and the mode transition time of the serving eNB and neighbour eNBs." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509402> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Update the texts so that there is no single target cell restriction for X2 based handover.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has isolated impact with the previous version of the specification (same release) because it impacts the S1/X2 based handover for NTN when a time-based trigger condition is used." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509403> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Update the texts so that there is no single target cell restriction for X2 based handover.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has isolated impact with the previous version of the specification (same release) because it impacts the S1/X2 based handover for NTN when a time-based trigger condition is used." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509405> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Added the possibility for the target node to update the stored SCG activation time after requesting the information from the UE." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509406> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Sections 4.10.1, 4.10.2, 4.10.3 are corrected according to the above.\n\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has an isolated impact towards the previous version of the specification (same release).\nThis CR has an impact on the NR Femto function." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509407> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "To clarify that the step 9a (Early Status Transfer) – step 22 (UE Context Release) can be performed multiple time for subsequent LTM.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has impact with the previous version of the specification (same release).\nThis CR has an impact under functional point of view.\nThe impact can be considered isolated because it impacts only LTM." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509408> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "To clarify that the step from Early Data Forwarding to step 29 can be performed multiple times for subsequent MCG LTM.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has impact with the previous version of the specification (same release).\nThis CR has an impact under functional point of view.\nThe impact can be considered isolated because it impacts only LTM." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509409> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Update the O&M Requirements to be applicable for both NTN regenerative payload and transparent payload." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509411> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the DL PDU Set Information Marking Support Indication in the description of PDU Set based QoS handling for DC case." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509412> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add “DL PDU Set Information Marking Support Indication” in the text regarding the PDU set handling in the handover case ." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509413> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In Area-specific SRS Configuration Activation Procedure, clarify how the semi-persistent UL-SRS is activated for the UE.\nIntroduce Semi-persistent Positioning SRS Deactivation Procedure in section 7.14.x.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has an impact from protocol and functional point of view. The impact can be considered isolated because it only impacts the activation/deactivation of the SP SRS transmission for positioning." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509414> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In Area-specific SRS Configuration Activation Procedure, clarify how the semi-persistent UL-SRS is activated for the UE.\nIntroduce Semi-persistent Positioning SRS Deactivation Procedure in section 7.14.x.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has an impact from protocol and functional point of view. The impact can be considered isolated because it only impacts the activation/deactivation of the SP SRS transmission for positioning." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509416> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1. Following Rel-15/16/17 DC procedures, a note is added to clarify the order for step 20 and step 21:\n- NOTE: The order the UE sends the MN RRCReconfigurationComplete* message (step 21) and performs the random access procedure towards the PSCell (step 20) is not defined. The successful random access procedure towards the target PSCell is not required for a successful completion of the RRC Reconfiguration procedure.\n2. In Figure 10.5.2-5, step 23 and 24 (SN modification request procedure) is changed optional as we did in Rel-18 for SN initiated subsequent CPAC. Text descriptions were added to clarify:\n- If the last serving SN is not configured as a candidate SN, the MN triggers the MN initiated SN Release procedure to inform the last serving SN to stop providing user data to the UE, and triggers the Xn-U Address Indication procedure to inform the last serving SN the address of the SN of the selected candidate PSCell and if applicable, starts normal data forwarding.\n\n3. In Figure 10.5.2-5 on the signaling flows, several IE names are corrected, descriptions for TCI state configuration are added, and related clarifications are included." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509417> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Added steps 11a and 11b in the inter-gNB LTM signalling flow to describe the CSI-RS Coordination procedure, and included a note indicating that the triggering of this procedure is implementation-specific.\nMiscellaneous corrections and updates." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509418> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify the NTN related parameters equivalent to the corresponding list specified in TS 38.300 shall be provided to the NTN eNB.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has impact on the functional point of view. The impact can be considered isolated because it clarifies the NTN parameters configured in the eNB is equivalent to the parameters configured in the gNB." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509419> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the MRO for PSCell addition failure for EN-DC." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509420> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add S-CPAC for the type of PSCell addition/change, .\nClarify the last serving node carry out the failure type of CHO with candidate SCG" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509421> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In 4.10.2.1, add the functionality of sending the NR Femto GW the UE CONTEXT RELEASE with the GW Context Release indication at successful Xn handover, to allow the NR Femto GW to release the UE context.\n\nIn 4.10.4, remove “IE” subffix for “cellReservedForOtherUse”." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509422> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add Ambient IoT related Network Identities." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509423> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Update the “A-IoT Session Release as defined in clause 16.x.8” to “A-IoT Session Release as defined in clause 16.23.8” in Figure 16.23.6-1.\nUpdate the Step 1 description from “Inventory procedure as specified in 16.x.6 step 1~6” to “Inventory procedure as specified in 16.23.6 step 1~6” in Figure 16.23.7-1.\nUpdate the Step 5 description from “A-IoT Session Release as defined in clause 16.x.8” to “A-IoT Session Release as defined in clause 16.23.8” in 16.23.6 step 1~6” in Figure 16.23.7-1.\nRefine the wording to reflect the AIoTF obtain the served reader ID list via OAM." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509424> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a note in section 9.2.5 to describe the solutions to avoid paging loss.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThus, this CR has isolated impact and is backwards compatible from a protocol point of view." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509425> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a note in section 9.2.5 to describe the solutions to avoid paging loss.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThus, this CR has isolated impact and is backwards compatible from a protocol point of view." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509426> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add a note in section 9.2.5 to describe the solutions to avoid paging loss.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThus, this CR has isolated impact and is backwards compatible from a protocol point of view." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509427> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Specify that the maximum number of subgroups is dependent on the PO-to-LO association which is defined in TS 38.331. And specify that the typical area in which the PO-to-LO association is the same is up to network configuration.\nSpecify that it is assumed that the same number of CN controlled subgroups is used at least within the registration area or the entire PLMN" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509428> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "-Removed the adjective “stationary” from the WAB clause 4.11." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509429> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add references to TS 38.300 on principles for AI/ML-assisted positioning with a gNB-side AI/ML model\nReflect that the Positioning Data Collected Needed IE is requested per measuring TRP in the UE positioning session.\nDefine meaning of “ground truth label”" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509430> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In clause 13.5.2, add a paragraph about the multi-modality service support.\nAdd clause 13.5.X, to capture the content about uplink rate control.\nAdd clause 13.5.y, to capture the content about the available bitrate monitoring." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509431> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Revise “Data Burst Size” as “Burst Size”.\nRemove “Indication of” in front of Burst Size and Time To Next Burst." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509432> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Stage 2 description is added to specify propagation of the MDT configuration during the Secondary Node Addition procedure.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThe CR has isolated impact.\nThe CR is backwards compatible from a protocol point of view." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509433> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Stage 2 description is added to specify propagation of the MDT configuration during the Secondary Node Addition procedure.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThe CR has isolated impact.\nThe CR is backwards compatible from a protocol point of view." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509434> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In the descriptions for Figure 9.2.3.5.2-2 (Signalling procedure for inter-gNB LTM), Step 3 and Step 5 are updated that the configuration of CSI-RS resources for early CSI acquisition is not based on a request from the source NG-RAN node." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509435> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "To use indicate/indication instead of reques;\nTo clarify that the gNB receiving request just needs to signal back SRS resource info to the gNB(s) which initiated the request." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509436> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the description for exchanging L2 reset ID and UE based TA measurement." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509437> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the description for exchanging L2 reset ID and UE based TA measurement." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509438> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Introduce Continuous Management-based MDT in the definitions.\nIntroduce immediate and logged MDT mode in MDT mode part.\nIntroduce the new section to describe the solution for continuous MDT measurement collection." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509440> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the description for Roaming and Access Restrictions transmission in Retrieve UE Context procedure.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThe CR has isolated impact.\nThe CR is backwards compatible from a protocol point of view." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509444> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The IE NR-DL-PRS-ProcessingCapability in IE NR-DL-AIML-ProvideCapabilities is replaced by an AI/ML positioning specific version (NR-DL-AIML-PRS-ProcessingCapability-r19), which includes only those PRS processing capabilities relevant to DL AI/ML Positioning.\nThe Editor's Notes are deleted.\nA NOTE is added to the field description for nr-TRP-RequestList indicating that this field is applicable to DL AI/ML Positioning only.\nA NOTE is added to the field description for IE NR-DL-PRS-QCL-ProcessingCapability that QCL indication for a PRS-only TP is not supported for DL AI/ML positioning.\nThe IE NR-TRP-LocationInfo-Implicit is revised according to RAN1 response LS in R2-2508010.\nDL-PRS Capabilities in RRC_INACTIVE/RRC_IDLE according to RAN1 feature list R1-2509584 (R2-2509386) are added." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509445> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "An IE SSR-ProviderInfo has been added to SSR Assistance Data components to align with RTCM Specification [30]. The IE contains the two fields SSR Provider ID and Solution ID as specified in RTCM Specification [30]." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509446> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The changes can be summarized as follows:\nAdd the abbreviation AI/ML: Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning\nChange “AS layer buffer” to “AS layer memory”\nRemove ‘OtherConfig’ in Step 3 of Clause 22.2.3\nUpdate “-\tIf its AI/ML functionality applicability status changes.” to “-\tIf its AI/ML functionality applicability status changes.”\nAdd a bracket to include AI/ML on definition from subclause 3.2 as\n“Supported (AI/ML) functionality: AI/ML functionality which can be indicated by using UE capability information.”\nUpdate:\nIf its AS buffer to log data for Network-side data collection becomes full, or reaches a threshold configured by the network;\nto\n-\tIf its AS layer memory to log data for Network-side data collection becomes full;\n-\tIf its AS layer memory to log data for Network-side data collection reaches a threshold configured by the network;\nUpdate clause 22.2.1 Introduction to add:\n“where the set of beams for prediction can be SSB or CSI-RS beams and another set of beams for measurement can be SSB or CSI-RS beams”\nUpgrade the level of subclause of “data collection for offline model training” so that the subclause for data collection is the same level as 22.1. Now it is “22.X\tData Collection for Offline Model Training”. Add two editorials as: “22.X.1 Network-side data collection applies only to AI/ML beam management feature.” and “22.X.2 UE-side data collection applies to AI/ML Beam management and CSI prediction features.\nCapture RAN2#132 agreement: “For RAN and OAM centric data collection in NR-DC scenario, the NW side data collection only can be configured for MCG.”\n”Some editorial corrections" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509448> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Multiple corrections based on R2-2508724." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509449> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "lpwus-OffsetPreferenceConfig is captured as per cell group configuration.\nClarify that if the UE has no preference on offset for LP-WUS monitoring of the cell group, the UE do not include timeOffset in the LPWUS-OffsetPreference IE.\nAdd the the missing part of “release lpwus-OffsetPreferenceConfig, if configured, and stop timer T346xx, if running;” in Section 5.3.7.3.\nAdd description of lpwus-OffsetPreferenceConfig in the field description of otherConfig.\nUpdate the below RRC parameters based on the lastest RAN1 RRC parameters in R2-2508022/R1-2508205:\nChange the field name of “lpwus-OffsetPreference” to “timeOffest”\nClarify that UAI reporting for UE’s preferred time offset for LP-WUS monitoring is actually used to report the preferred time offset for RRC_CONNECTED.\nUpdate the value for lpwus-OffsetFirstMoWithinLo, lpwus-NominalMoDuration, lpwus-ActualDuration, lpss-BinarySeqIndex in LowPowerConfig-r19 in DownlinkConfigCommonSIB.\nUpdate the value for lpwus-TimeOffset1-1, lpwus-TimeOffset1-2, lpwus-MO-1-1, lpwus-MO-1-2, lpwus-NumOfMO-1-1, lpwus-NumOfMO-1-2, lpwus-TCI-States, lpwus-NominalMoDuration, lpwus-ActualDuration, lpwus-NumOfBits, lpwus-PDCCH-MonitoringTimer in LPWUS-Config in PhysicalCellGroupConfig.\nAdd Need code for startSymbol2-r19 in lpss-StartSymbol-r19.\nAdd Need code for lpss-OverlaidSeqRoot-r19\nAdd IE lpwus-NumOfBits\nChange the “low power receiver” to “LP-WUR” or “low power wake-up receiver”\nClarify that the lpwus-PDCCH-MonitoringTimer configuration for secondary DRX group is smaller than or equal to that for the default DRX group.\nThe field timer2 is optinal present for lpwus-PDCCH-MonitoringTimer, add the corresponding condition for timer2.\nLP-WUS and paging adaptation can be configured and used together. Introduce a separate lpwus-LoFrameOffsetList configuration for LP-WUS with paging adaptation.\nAdd ‘Network does not configure csi-Mask when lpwus-PDCCH-MonitoringTimer is configured (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 10.4D)’ in the field description of csi-Mask.\nSome editorial changes and typo have been fixed." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509450> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarify that when UE determine whether it’s not in DRX active time, UE should consider LP-WUS impact when evaluating all DRX Active Time conditions." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509453> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Following changes:\nUE adjusts SMTC received in the RRCRelease message according to the actual propagation delay\nRemoving the maxFFS and replacing it with more suitable type constraint\nThe need code in the conditional presence of SIB19 is fixed" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509454> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Moved sentence related to codepoints to general part instead of the same sentence twice for CN controlled and UE_ID based subgrouping\nSimilar clarification as for when DCP is not monitored is captured for LP-WUS in connected mode, that is LP-WUS is not monitored in active time, during BWP switching, measurement gaps, MUSIM gaps or when waiting for reply for CFRA preamble after beam failure detection.\nAdded missing text in part about LP-WUS and paging adaptation.\nAdded low mobility condition to entry condition of serving cell relaxation and offloading, together with an Editor’s note to mention related further open issue.\nAdded text related to LP-WUS disable indication and reference to new text in this same specification in 9.2.2.1.\nClarified the cases where UE monitors common codepoint for LP-WUS and common codepoint or UEs subgroup ID is not found.\nEditorial corrections." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509455> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "- LP-WUS may be transmitted on a subset of the transmitted beams as indicated in lpwus-LPSS-BeamSubset-r19. To clarify that the transmitted beams are configured for LP-WUS.\n- Clarify that the UE uses corresponding parameter if the UE supporting paging adaptation and LP-WUS while corresponding parameters for paging adaptation with LP-WUS is signalling in system information.\n- Clarify that further relaxed neighbouring measurements is applied, to align the corresponding description in stage 2.\n- When the exit condition for serving cell measurement offloading is fulfilled, the UE is required to stop serving cell measurement offloading.\n- Clarify in TS 38.304 how to determine the value of frame level offset according to the received lpwus-LoFrameOffsetList according to the RAN1 LS (R2-2508020).\n- Update how the UE determines whether to monitors with LP-WUS and which LO is monitored in TS 38.304 according to the RAN1 LS (R2-2508020).\n- Capture that LP-WUS monitoring can be disabled according to NAS signalling according to SA2 LS (S2-2511295) in Nov SA2 meeting." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509456> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1. In clause 5.2, correct UE behaviour for TAT expiry for UE-initiated CSI reporting and multi-panel SDM UL transmission.\n2. In clause 5.7, correct how to determine DRX active time taking into account mode-A UE Initiated Report Indication.\n3. In clause 5.15.1, correct UE behavior for BWP deactivation for UE-initiated CSI reporting.\n4. In clause 5.18.3 and 6.1.3.13, clarify the existing Aperiodic CSI Trigger State Subselection MAC CE is used for CSI trigger state subselection for UEI-CSI reporting.\n5. In clause 5.30, specify UE behaivor for UE-initiated CSI reporting in FR2 UL gap." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509457> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Clarification for Single hop and multi-hop type differentiation in 5.8.3.2.\nClarification that SL-RelayUE-ConfigMH IE is appliacable only during multi hop relay communication in 6.3.5\nClarification that Last relay UE monitors PO based on sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE or sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE-List in 5.3.2 and 5.8.9.8\nClarification that both single and multi hop L3 U2N Relay UE shall perform RLF handling in 5.3.10\nAdditional new condition in 5.3.3.1a and 5.3.13.1a for UE to initiate RRC setup or resume to transmit L2 multihop relay discovery message if sl-L2U2N-MH-Relay is included in in SIB12\nRemoval of L2 Intermediate U2N Relay UE related description from 5.3.3.4\nAligning the wording for upper layer handling and sending of the NotificationMessageSidelink message in 5.3.3, 5.3.10. 5.3.15.\nRemoval of unnecessary differtiation of First U2N Relay and Intermediate U2N Relay in 5.3.3.8\nClarification on the relationship between L2 U2N Relay UE and L2 Last U2N Relay UE that L2 U2N Relay UE is used in case of single hop.\nAddition of new condition for sl-L2U2N-MH-Relay during SUI initiation for MH case 5.8.3.2\nAddition of sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE-List in 5.8.9.8.2 and 5.8.9.8.3\nAddition of sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE-List in 5.8.9.8.3\nClarification that for Intermediate relay UE, the Paging/SIB associated with the downstream remote UEs may comes from Parent instead of the network in 5.8.9.9\nClarification on reception of the UuMessageTransferSidelink by the L2 Intermediate U2N Relay UE in 5.8.9.9.4\nClarification for the field description for timers T300/T301/T319 for multi-hop relay when the timers field for remote UE are absent\nChanging relayUE-RRCState-r19 from Enumerated to seprate IE\nMinor Correction/Clarification in procedural text, field descriptions and ASN.1 (X504, E046, O509, O510, E049, H456)\n\nFollowing changes are made based on the agreed ToDo RILs in RAN 2#131 bis and other agreements\nAddion of the additional discovery transmission threshold condition\nAddion of missing conditions of SUI initiation for discovery transmission at the intermediate relay and last relay\nAdding the condition that Intermediate relay UE in any state can trigger a notification message after receiving release message from its parent\nAdding the condition that intermediate relay UE can be triggered to transmit the notification message towards the child UE upon intermediate Relay UE's RRC connection/Resume failure\nClarification that MH remote UE will report its own SRC L2 ID to network\nIntroduce a paging ID list in SL-TxResourceReqL2U2N-Relay-r17\nRevise Figure 5.8.9.8.1-1 to support the transmission of the RemoteUEInformationSidelink message to both the remote UE and the child UE\nAlign the procedural text to use the name mh-IndicationType instead of IndicationType\nAdd RemoteUEInformationSidelink transmission behaviour for RRC_CONNECTED intermediate relay UE\nInclude the condition in the note 4 in 5.8.15.3 that the note is only applicable to multi-hop L2 U2N Relay communication.\nAdd an indication in the measurement report to indicate the hop status of the candidate relay UE (single-hop or multihop)\nAdd the handling that L2 Intermediate U2N Relay UE in RRC_IDLE/ RRC_INACTIVE detects sidelink radio link failure with its child UE should initiate the Remote UE information to its parent UE.\nAdd the condition that for discovery model B, an intermediate relay UE that already has a PC5 connection with a parent UE may send a response message directly to the remote UE s provided the PC5 AS conditions with the child UE are met.\nMinor Editroial corrections for procedure text\n\nFollowing changes are made based on the agreed RILs in RAN 2#132\nUpdate the procedure texts in clause 5.3.5.15.2 and 5.3.5.15.3, with respect to releasing, adding/ modifying the configurations of indirectly connected child UEs\nClarify setting of hop type as single-hop or multi-hop depending on whether the offered relay service by the candidate relay is single-hop or multi-hop in 5.5.5.1\nClarify in 5.8.3.3 that L2 U2N Last Relay UE in RRC_CONNECTED state includes sl-PagingIdentityRemoteUEList in SUI if there at least one Paging ID from an indirect child under the reported SL Destination to be reported to gNB.\nClarify that when an Intermediate Relay UE intends to report any of its child UE in SUI message, the UE shall indicate “UE-type” as “relayUE” and include both upstream and downstream SL destinations in the sl-TxResourceReqListCommRelay" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509458> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Introduction of new SIBxy which include IoT NTN neighbour cell information, i.e., IoT NTN carrier frequency and satellite information." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509460> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Implements the discussion in post meeting discussion for R19 RRC ASN1 review after RAN2#131bis." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509461> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Enhancing the text related to Continuous MDT in clause 16.20.4 by adding a reference to TS 37.320.\nAdding TS 37.320 to the list of referenced specifications in Section 2.\n\nImpact Analysis:\nImpact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release):\nThis CR has isolated impact as it only impacts the Continuous Management-based MDT functionality." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509462> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following changes were made:\n-\tEditorial changes, e.g. italicized field values, inconsistencies in field names between ASN.1 and procedural text, etc.;\n-\tIntroducing a new list for reporting logged data for network-side data collection to avoid repeating the logging configuration ID for every measurement entry;\n-\tChanging some fields in ASN.1 from optional to mandatory;\n-\tChanging some field names for clarity;\n-\tRephrasing some procedural text for clarity, better alignment with legacy cases, and better alignment with draft capability descriptions;\n-\tSome modifications to the ASN.1 content and structure of the event-triggered CSI logging configuration and of the parameters for prediction, UE-side data collection and monitoring within CSI-ReportConfig;\n-\tIntroducing a new IE in HandoverPreparationInformation message to convey applicability information;\n-\tIntroducing a new flag to disable applicability reports for beam management prediction configurations in CSI-ReportConfig;\n-\tClarifying in the procedural text that a periodic CSI report configuration for prediction is submitted to the lower layers only if it is reported by the UE as applicable in RRCReconfigurationComplete\n-\tRemoving the definition of “Applicable AI/ML configuration”;\n-\tRenumbering clause “5.5a Logged Measurements for Network-Side Data Collection” (and the subclauses within) as “5.5c Logged Measurements for Network-Side Data Collection”." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509463> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the LP-WUS Disable Indication in the Core Network Assistance Information IE provided by AMF.\nAdd the LP-WUS Disable Indication in the XnAP RAN paging message.\nList bullets for each IE in the CN assistance information for readability.\nSimplify sentences on XnAP RAN paging.\nAdd the Further Extended UE Identity Index Value in the XnAP RAN Paging message.\nAdd the Further Extended UE Identity Index Value in the Core Network Assistance Information and the condition for AMF to send it to gNB." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509464> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "The following RILs are implemented: A200, C002, C007, C008, C009, E010, E011, E012, E013, E014, H250, H252, H255, H256, H257, N086, O710, Q200, S024, S025, S026, S027, V202, V206, V208, Y001, Z253, Z254.\n\nIn addition, Class0 RILs have been implemented (33, 70, and 75) and the following agreements from RAN2#131bis are included:\n[V208] Confirm that bitmap is used to indicate the N closest reference location\nFor [H252] we add the “N closest…” in the procedural text.\n[H250] Use “closest reference location information” to replace “location information” in the UAI reporting procedures, and clarify that this this information is for “assisted SMTC and measurement gap configuration”.\n[S024] Reporting close reference locations in RRCReconfigurationComplete message is not mandatory to UE. UE only includes the report in RRCReconfigurationComplete when it is available\n[Q200] We specify that smtc5 with multiple offsets is not broadcast in a Earth-moving cell scenario (to be captured in the smtc5 field description in system information)\n[C008] We change the limitation as “The total number of configurable SMTCs offsets across smtc4list and smtc5list is 6.”\n[C009] RAN2 understands that if the NW wants to reuse the periodicity in smtc1, the NW needs to configure smtc4 (we capture something accordingly in the field description)\n[V206] Change the need code for mbs-SessionAreaList-r19 from Need R to Need S.\n[V206] Add in the FD of mbs-SessionAreaList-r19 that UE considers the associated service can be received within the entire cell area if the list is absent\n[O710] Fix the description for warningMessageSegmentType in SIB7.\n\nThe following agreements from RAN2#132 are captured:\n[A200] Extend the entry number of RefLocList-r19 to 7 so that the Rel-15 smtc in SIB2/SIB4 can be associated with a reference location as well.\n[H256] If an SMTC5 intends to reuse the full SMTC4 configuration, an SSB-MTC5-r19 should appear in smtc5list and have empty child IEs (exact wording can be further discussed).\n[E056] (TP in R2-2509220 is used as a baseline):\nThe set of (frequency-independent) reference locations is included in SIB19\nFrequency-specific reference locations can be indicated by signaling a frequency-specific offset, e.g., for longitude and latitude.\nIn RRC_CONNECTED state, the UE reports the N closest reference locations from a single set of reference locations, either provided via dedicated RRC signaling or, otherwise, provided in SIB19.\n[Y001]: We clarify the smtc4list, smtc5list field description as follows: For a UE that supports less SMTCs than what is included in smtc4list and smtc5list, it is up to the UE to select which SMTCs to consider, for which the UE may use location information in refLocList, if present.\n[H255]: clarifying the smtc5list field description as follows: “If an entry in smtc5list is present but the pci-List and/or offset fields are absent, the UE applies the value of the corresponding field from the entry at the same position in smtc4list, if present, and the periodicity value in smtc5list. If an entry in smtc5list is present but its fields are absent, the UE applies the values from the entry at the same position in smtc4list.”\nChange the terminology Assisted-SSB-MTC-Config-r19 to Assisted-SSB-MTC-MG-Config-r19\n[E011] Add: “and, for MBS ISA capable UEs, are located within the Intended Service Area associated with the MBS service, if any.”\n[V206] change the field description of mbs-SessionAreaList to “if this field is absent, the MBS broadcast service can be received within the MBS service area”." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509465> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "“location measurements” in the description is replaced by “location information”.\nThe unit \"meters\" is changed to \"metres\".\n\"device\" is changed to \"target device\".\nThe field description for refEphReq is completed." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509466> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Adding reference to 36.102 for parameters carrierFreq and carrierFreqOffset in SIB27\nRemoving the NeighSatelliteInfoListNB-r19" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509468> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "New Release-19 capabilities from RAN1/4 are added based on the latest RAN1/4 feature lists.\nR1-2509584 Updated RAN1 UE features list for Rel-19 NR after RAN1 #123 EoM\nR4-2522332 Rel-19 RAN4 UE feature list for NR (version 4)\n\nThe following RAN2 endorsed CRs are included:\nR2-2507588 Corrections on AI air UE capability\nR2-2507722 Correction on 38306 for UE capability for Mob Ph4\nR2-2507840 Corrections on SONMDT UE Capabilities\nR2-2508484 Draft 38.306 CR for Rel-19 XR UE capabilities\nR2-2509174\tIntroduction of UE capability on low band CA via switching\nR2-2508992\tCorrection on NES UE capability for paging adaption\nR2-2508444\tCorrections on Rel-19 NR NTN UE capabilities\nR2-2509214 Introduction of NTN Ku Band\nR2-2509441 Correction to R19 LP-WUS UE Capabilities" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509469> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "New Release-19 capabilities from RAN1/4 are added based on the latest RAN1/4 feature lists.\nR1-2509584 Updated RAN1 UE features list for Rel-19 NR after RAN1 #123 EoM\nR4-2522332 Rel-19 RAN4 UE feature list for NR (version 4)\n\nThe following RAN2 endorsed CRs are included:\nR2-2507721 Correction on 38331 for UE capability for Mob Ph4\nR2-2507839 Corrections on SONMDT UE Capabilities\nR2-2509173\tIntroduction of UE capability on low band CA via switching\nR2-2508443\tCorrections on Rel-19 NR NTN UE capabilities\nR2-2509215\tIntroduction of NTN Ku Band\nR2-2509442 Corrections on Rel-19 RAN1 UE capability" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509470> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In clause 6.12.1, clarify the purpose of two closed loop power control adjustment states." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509471> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In clause 3.1, add missing sentence “The child UE is the U2N Remote UE in case of single-hop L2 U2N Relay communication.”\nIn clause 4.2.2, add space between “theChild” in Figure 4.2.2-2.\nIn clause 5.2.2.0/5.2.2.2, add last relay operation for identifying SRB0 of the Child UE.\nIn clause 5.2.3, remove “or sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL”.\nIn clause 5.2.3.3.2, change “sl-EgressRLC-Channel-UL” to “sl-EgressRLC-Channel-DL”.\nIn clause 5.3.3.2, add the using of SL-RLC1 when the corresponding dedicated configuration is not provided." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509472> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "“i:th” is included in the definition of non-delay-reporting PDCP SDU.\nTypos “Duplicte discarding” is corrected to “Duplicate discarding” in Figures 4.2.2-1 and 4.2.2-2.\nA NOTE is added to clarify that for AM DRBs the UE can (re)send the PDCP SN gap report when upper layer requests a PDCP entity re-establishment." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509473> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1st change: We suggest to increase the bullet levels of the highlighted text by one step (i.e., to be performed under 1> for each measConfigAppLayerId received from upper layers.)\n\n2nd change: In order to remove highlighted text, we suggest clarification to differentiate 1) encoded message for SRB4 transmission and 2) encoded message for SRB5 transmission." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509474> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "1st change: We suggest to increase the bullet levels of the highlighted text by one step (i.e., to be performed under 1> for each measConfigAppLayerId received from upper layers.)\n\n2nd change: In order to remove highlighted text, we suggest clarification to differentiate 1) encoded message for SRB4 transmission and 2) encoded message for SRB5 transmission." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509475> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Description of assistance information for cell selection/idle mobility to NR NTN from IoT NTN (BL UEs, UE in CEs and NB-IoT UE connected to E-UTRAN over NTN)" .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509476> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "To support UE mapping the different reference locations with multiple eventD2 and reporting subsequent measurement result fulfills eventD2 entering/leaving condition:\n1. In clause 5.5.4.15a, clarify that the moving reference location is determined based on the physical cell identity (i.e. eventD2PhysCellld as defined within reportConfigNR), if present.\n2. In clause 6.3.2, add an eventD2PhysCellId-r19 IE and corresponding field description in ReportConfigNR.\n3. In clause 6.3.3, add a UE capability eventD2-MultiReferenceLocations-r19 in MeasAndMobParameters.\n\n\nImpact analysis\nImpacted 5G architecture options:\nStandalone\nImpacted functionality:\nNR-NTN, Measurement\n\nInter-operability:\n1.\t if the network supports the change and the UE does not, UE is unable to report subsequent measurement result fulfills eventD2 entering/leaving condition when multiple NTN earth-moving cells are configured.\n\n2.\t if the UE supports the change and the network does not, UE is unable to report subsequent measurement result fulfills eventD2 entering/leaving condition when multiple NTN earth-moving cells are configured." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509477> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "Add the stage 2 description for the optional PLMN list for geographical area scope for MDT in NTN and modify the stage 2 description for the geographical area." .
<https://w3id.org/spectra/inst/RAN2/Tdoc/tdoc:R2-2509478> spectra:sourceAuthoredSummary "In clause 6.3.7, added a clarification on notification configuration for MBMS-dedicated cell regarding usage of additional non-MBSFN subframes to the field description of notificationSF-Index." .
